adjudication.rationale:
In addGuests.handler.ts, the email-sending step is wrapped in a try/catch that swallows all errors:

```ts
try {
  await sendAddGuestsEmails(evt, guests);
} catch (err) {
  console.log("Error sending AddGuestsEmails");
}

return { message: "Guests added" };
```

Because the catch does not rethrow or otherwise signal failure, the TRPC mutation will resolve successfully even if sendAddGuestsEmails (which uses Promise.all and would throw on any send failure) fails. On the client, this will trigger the `onSuccess` toast (`guests_added`) and close the dialog, so the user is never informed that notification emails were not sent.
